{"id": "swebq0196", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 14888815, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "when do they change the time in california?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0196.wav", "input_sha256": "47dfb1fcddb36de471c568edd74285c50342863eec78e2c3a492d8d22045b375", "input_samples": 34905, "input_s": 2.182, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.8334, "act": 0.9985, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "In California, the clocks change twice a year: Spring forward: Sunday, March 8, 2026 at 2:00 AM — clocks move ahead to 3:00 AM. , Fall back: Sunday, November 1, 2026 at 2:00 AM — clocks move back to 1:00 AM. (timeanddate.com) In general, California changes time on the second Sunday in March and the first Sunday in November.", "expert_answer": "In **California**, the clocks change twice a year:\n\n- **Spring forward:** **Sunday, March 8, 2026 at 2:00 AM** — clocks move ahead to **3:00 AM**.\n- **Fall back:** **Sunday, November 1, 2026 at 2:00 AM** — clocks move back to **1:00 AM**. ([timeanddate.com](https://www.timeanddate.com/time/change/usa/california?utm_source=openai))\n\nIn general, California changes time on the **second Sunday in March** and the **first Sunday in November**.", "transcript": "When do they change the time in California?\n", "asr_s": 0.45, "expert_s": 5.36, "expert_input_samples": 34905, "expert_input_s": 2.182, "expert_input_sha256": "47dfb1fcddb36de471c568edd74285c50342863eec78e2c3a492d8d22045b375", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.0, "relay_synth_ms": 15278, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 14, "feed_lag_max_ms": 701, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 1349, "audio_fil